  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 334 AM EDT Sun Jul 5 2026\n\nSlightly above normal high and low temperatures are forecast this \nweek along with daily rain chances more typical of a summertime \npattern.\n\nBroad troughing will be over the eastern US through mid-week then \nflow becomes more zonal over Georgia for the latter half of the \nweek. Models continue to indicate above normal moisture over the \narea most days fueling thunderstorm development mainly in the \nafternoon and evenings. Storm coverage will likely be isolated to \nscattered each day with NBM PoPs consistently bringing higher values \nto far northwest GA where ensemble guidance favors the highest QPF \ntotals for the period.\n\nWhile temperatures trend down from the weekend, hot conditions are \nstill expected to continue with highs mainly in the 90s and lows in \nthe 70s, with lower values in the mountains. Dewpoints remain \nelevated bringing heat index values mainly in the upper 90s to low \n100s, though some locations in the far southeast may still approach \nthe 105 degree mark.",
